title: January 1928
subtitle: The Federation meets
tags: event
view-if: year = 1928 and month = 2
priority: 3
max-visits: 1

Nine years after the Federation came together, the Farmer-Labor Party holds its winter convention. Socialists from the immigrant wards, farmers from the plains, railroad brotherhoods and progressive reformers crowd into a single hall, and for once nobody can find a majority without the others.

The Conservative Republicans still hold most of Congress, and a Republican-Democratic coalition governs on both sides of the aisle when it suits them. But in the House the Federation now holds the balance of power. The question, this year, is what to do with it.
